Description: system-wide DNS blocking of ads, trackers, malware and phishing
 blockads-linux filters every DNS query of the computer against the filter
 lists of blockads-android (StevenBlack, EasyPrivacy, URLhaus, ...). A
 sandboxed local resolver answers on a privileged loopback port; while
 protection is on, iptables rules redirect outgoing DNS to it. Routing,
 resolv.conf and NetworkManager are never modified, the rules are never
 saved, and any failure removes them so DNS keeps working (fail-open).
 .
 It includes a Qt6 GUI with a tray icon and the blockadsctl command.
 Lists are downloaded from their original publishers and compiled locally;
 there is no telemetry.
